---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Component Usage Overview">
  <h1>🧩 Component Usage Overview</h1>
  <p>This page helps visualize and plan which components should be loaded at the <b>top</b>, <b>middle</b>, and <b>bottom</b> of each page. Use this as a checklist and planning tool for DRY, maintainable layouts.</p>
  <hr />
  <h2>Top of Page</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>CommonImports.astro</code> (shared imports)</li>
    <li><code>BaseLink.astro</code> (internal link logic)</li>
    <li><code>Header</code> / Navigation components</li>
    <li>Any global context providers (if used)</li>
  </ul>
  <hr />
  <h2>Middle of Page</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Page-specific content components (e.g., blog post, project details)</li>
    <li>Lists (e.g., <code>SitemapList.astro</code>)</li>
    <li>Visualizations (e.g., <code>ImportRelationships.jsx</code>, <code>TreeMap.jsx</code>, <code>FileRelationships.jsx</code>)</li>
    <li>Markdown content (from <code>.md</code> or <code>.mdx</code> files)</li>
  </ul>
  <hr />
  <h2>Bottom of Page</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>CommonFooterImports.astro</code> (shared footer imports)</li>
    <li>Footer component (copyright, links)</li>
    <li>Any analytics or tracking scripts (if needed)</li>
  </ul>
  <hr />
  <h2>How to Use This Page</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the lists above to plan what should be included in each section of your pages.</li>
    <li>Audit existing pages to see which components they use and where.</li>
    <li>Update this page as your conventions evolve.</li>
  </ul>
  <hr />
  <p><i>Generated on: 2025-06-22</i></p>
</Layout>
